WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.010
Episode 19

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.010
The Ghost of the Old Castle, King Boom Boo

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.860
We're okay over here.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.820
Listen. This is a very calm scene, so concentrate on your emotions.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.950
Don't try to fake it with mere facial expressions.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.160
Same goes for you. Don't exaggerate more than you did during rehearsal.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.790
Oops, it's still a bit blurry.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.800
Ella?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.880
What's with that outfit?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.050
Are you also going to be in the movie?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.970
Yes. They advertised for extras at the nearby village, but no one was interested.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.850
Do I look good?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.390
We're going to start filming.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.560
No! Take me with you!

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.860
Don't leave me behind!

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.940
Wait, Ashley! Wait!

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.160
Cut! Okay!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.000
Your mom is amazing, Chris.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.870
Chris, are you having a good time?

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:12.580
Yeah!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.840
Where are your friends? You said you were bringing them.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.460
Hello.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:25.810
Oh my, that's well made! Is that a present from the special effects team?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.390
She doesn't know about us?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:35.690
This is just how my mom is. By the way, where did Cream and the others go?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.110
Beats me.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.440
What's this?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.400
Stop!

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.740
Right there.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.950
Are they animals?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.450
We can easily erase them digitally later.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.960
You're right. Please take care of it.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.340
Alright, let's go to the next scene!

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.640
Let's watch from here.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.810
Start rehearsal!

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:19.280
Dear, please wait! Don't go! Please dear!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.370
What is this? It's in the way.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.960
Wait a sec. Let me try pulling the camera back.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.470
What was that?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.470
Wait! Don't go, dear!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.890
It's still no good.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.770
There.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.820
Start the take!

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.530
Ready...

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.410
Action!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.690
I'm sorry, but there's noise.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:42.780
Cut!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.830
I was nervous.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.960
Strange, I don't see anything wrong.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:03.920
How is it?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.420
Everything seems fine.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.010
Then let's start take two.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.480
I'm sorry, but there's noise.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.940
Cut! Again? Let's call it a day.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.540
That was a long day for you, mom.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.870
Chris, you're still up?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
Yeah. I wanted to say goodnight to you, mom.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.580
Chris!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.380
Goodnight, Chris.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.630
Goodnight, mom.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.220
See you later.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.680
Good luck tomorrow, mom.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.600
Thank you, Chris.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.180
I wonder what that noise was?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.110
Where's everyone?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.650
Amy and the others went to Ella's room.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.200
Sonic also?

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.580
No, I don't know about Sonic.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.830
I wonder where Sonic went.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.640
It's from around here.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.320
I hear children's voices.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.410
Chris?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.420
I know it's you, Chris. Stop hiding and come out!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.180
How strange. Am I hearing things?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.770
Maybe I'm tired.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.020
Chris.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.570
The moon.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.280
This side is the sun.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.240
What does it mean?

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:47.750
Lindsey! Lindsey! Where are you?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.670
Mom!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.880
Mrs. Thorndyke, where are you?

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.840
- Chris's mom, where did you go?

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.880
Chris's mom!

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.260
What? What's the matter?

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.230
What? What's that voice?

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.520
The sound is coming from the other side of the wall.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.530
Mrs. Thorndyke, is that you?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.780
I'll go get help!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.500
Amy?

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.050
What's wrong, Amy?

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.970
Quick, help me!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.310
Ella! Cream! Cheese!

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.770
What's wrong?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.230
Weird ghosts pulled Ella, Cream and Cheese into the wall!

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:55.570
Ghosts?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.080
Why you…

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.500
What's that?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.550
Damn, my punches can't hit them!

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.640
Tails!

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.560
Oh no!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.810
Sonic!

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.270
Chris!

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.780
What's this?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:44.410
The pedestal in the yard! There must be something there that relates to this!

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.250
Sonic!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.160
Give Sonic back!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.290
Sonic!

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.170
Everybody!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.810
Sonic...

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.290
The entire staff searched for her all night, but we couldn't find her anywhere.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.700
Just as I thought.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:34.710
'Just as I thought?' Did something like this happen before?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:35.840
Yes.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.340
Here it is.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:43.220
Someone must have removed it.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:47.720
Yeah, you might be right. There's something written here.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:52.560
'Appears under the moon. Disappears under the sun'?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.060
I wonder what it means.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.360
What is it?

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:06.330
There's a breeze coming from below the pedestal. There might be something underneath here.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:12.210
Stairs?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.170
So there is something underneath.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.840
Sonic must be there too.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.460
Let's go.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.640
It's dangerous! Besides, we don't know what's down there.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.140
What do you think you're doing?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:32.230
Well... The policemen are here, so everyone can search together.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.270
Amy!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.520
Sheesh...

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.740
I thought you were scared.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.870
Of course I'm scared. Aren't you scared too, Amy?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.330
Not at all!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:20.440
I'm thinking of living on my own someday by renting a cheap apartment in Station Square.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:25.070
And I don't care if it's small, but I want to open a diner called Amy's Kitchen.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.780
Sounds good.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.210
Is that a magic charm?

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.380
Maybe...

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.140
Alright, I'll defeat them with this!

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.680
Amy, wait!

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.230
Where are we?

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:07.900
Is this the basement of the castle? More importantly, I wonder where they disappeared to.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.280
Amy, over there!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.850
Let's go, Amy.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.310
Okay.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.400
Sonic?

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.450
Is there anything here?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.500
Where are those guys?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.080
It's strange. I'm sure they came in here.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.790
Sonic?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.510
Sonic?

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:10.090
Amy! Chris! Over here!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.090
Sonic!

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.720
Both of you, be careful!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.970
Amy, my love.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.560
What are you saying all of a sudden?

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:23.690
Do me a favor. Place that hourglass into the hole in the wall.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:27.070
Understood. You want me to insert this.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.160
Over there!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.410
Amy!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.210
Amy? What's up? What are you planning to do?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.830
Is this the place?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:49.170
Yes, Amy. Place the hourglass into the hole with the moon symbol facing upwards.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.720
Moon symbol...

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:52.800
It's this side!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.140
You shouldn't do this, Amy.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.140
It'll be fine because Sonic says so.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.640
Don't do it, Amy!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.600
I love you, Amy.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:07.860
Oh Sonic, Chris heard that too. How embarrassing.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.800
Who is that?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.560
I love you, Amy.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.020
The voice I heard wasn't Sonic's?

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.940
No. That monster was mimicking me!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:55.160
How horrible! How dare you play with a girl's emotions!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.330
I won't forgive you!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.920
Amy!

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.960
Let me go!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.260
Amy.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:28.560
Amy, are you all right?

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.610
I'm going to sacrifice you to King Boo-boo.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.740
No way!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.710
Come to your senses, Amy!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.130
Sonic! Help!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.760
Chris! Get me out of here!

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.890
Amy, stop!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.950
If I remember correctly...

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:24.080
Yes, Amy. Place the hourglass into the hole with the moon symbol facing upwards.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:28.500
The symbols on the hourglass are the moon and the sun.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.750
'Appears under the moon. Disappears under the sun.'

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.800
I get it!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.130
When the moon rises, they appear!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.350
When the sun rises, they disappear!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.200
Are you all right, Amy?

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.410
Sonic? Sonic!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.750
Hey, this isn't the time for this!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.210
You guys!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.250
Let's fight!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.010
I won't forgive you!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.360
What are you complaining for?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:44.070
I'm the one who has the right to complain!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.920
Mom! Mom!

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:01.590
Chris?

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.220
Oh, good morning everyone.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.560
'Good morning' isn't the right thing to say.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:08.970
Chris!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.890
Run away while you still can!

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:11.890
Sonic!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:13.730
I got it!

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.410
Oh yeah! You guys go ahead.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.060
See ya!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.230
Hurry. We only have a little further to go.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.110
But my feet hurt, so I can't walk.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.280
What? You're still here?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.490
Sonic, what about that guy?

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.820
Don't worry. I beat him.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.410
What?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.840
Damn! It's persistent!

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.140
Chris, hurry up!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:32.020
Why you!

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.570
Which side did I place upwards?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:50.740
The moon is facing upwards.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.500
Will this all be okay?

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.700
Don't mind.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.120
Was this a film shoot?

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.500
Was the next film supposed to be a fantasy movie?

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.210
Hey!

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:06.930
Lindsey, I'm glad you're okay.

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:09.390
Did something happen?

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:13.100
I'm surprised you guys escaped him.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:16.390
Him? You mean you know about that ghost?

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:21.270
My grandfather told me about him.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:31.070
My grandfather said that when he was a child, he and his friend went into the forest to look for something legendary...

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.170 --> 00:25:35.360
Departure! Egg Fort II
